<div class="phead chart"><div class="w"><ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="{{ PathBase }}/">Home</a></li><li>When to call</li></ol><p class="kick">The four-step ladder</p><h1>Not sure whether to call, come in, or dial 911?</h1><p class="lede">General information from a fictional practice, not medical advice. For emergencies call 911.</p></div></div><section class="sec tight"><div class="w"><div class="ladder"><div class="rung" style="--c:#58773a"><span class="n">STEP 1</span><h3>Care at home</h3><p>Rest, fluids and the steps in the guide.</p></div><div class="rung" style="--c:#2f6f9f"><span class="n">STEP 2</span><h3>Call the office</h3><p>Call us; a nurse asks a few questions.</p></div><div class="rung" style="--c:#c98a12"><span class="n">STEP 3</span><h3>Same-day visit</h3><p>Call at 8:00 am for a held slot.</p></div><div class="rung" style="--c:#d9503a"><span class="n">STEP 4</span><h3>Emergency</h3><p>Call 911. Do not wait for a call back.</p></div></div>
<div class="er" style="margin-top:28px"><b>Call 911</b> for chest pain, trouble breathing, signs of a stroke, severe bleeding or thoughts of harming yourself (or call or text 988).</div></div></section>
